  "frame": "Anatomical reference frame, same as the site (body-motion.ts): x = left-right (+x = subject Left, -x = Right); y = superior-inferior (+y = up); z = anterior-posterior (+z = anterior/front). Right-handed.",
  "angles": "Every movement has a unit axis and a range [0,max] measured in that movement own direction. A positive angle is a right-hand rotation about axis (flexion axis +x moves a point on the face forward and down; extension is the opposite axis). Translations (unit mm) move along axis. A movement and its opposite share one axis line with the sign flipped.",
  "signsInCode": "BodyPose in body-motion.ts: flexion + = flexion (rotation about +x), rotation + = turn to the Left (about +y), sideBend + = bend to the Left (about -z). codeMapping records this per movement.",
